  m_text: The ball valve operates pneumatically or electrically or manually. The
    ball of the valve opens or closes the fluid flow by turning the handle/actuator
    at 90 degrees clockwise or anticlockwise direction respectively. It starts the
    flow when the hole of the ball becomes parallel to the direction of the fluid
    flow. The ball stops the fluid flow as the wrench handle is turned anticlockwise
    up to 90 degrees. The ball valve cannot be operated in an intermediate state.
    Let us explore its working operation in detail.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e63ac0177aeed334f9a24408402d8fb6, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 1749380657243123591, guid: e63ac0177aeed334f9a24408402d8fb6,
